title: planet_descriptions
---
Barren but rich in minerals. Many have tried to settle here.
Rocky world with a nitrogen-oxygen atmosphere. Great landmasses are separated by oceans, with large climate variations depending on latitude.
The surface is hostile, but the core is valuable.
Endless storms sweep the land, making survival a temporary thing.
Once inhabited. Now only ruins remain.
A mining world stripped to its bones.
Cold, distant, and unforgiving.
There are signs of life. None are recent.
It offers resources at a cost few can afford.
The ground itself resists change.
Colonies spring up fast here.
Nothing grows. Everything erodes.
A world that feels abandoned, even when occupied.
===
